{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1094864-awakening-how-to-describe-it","id":1094864,"title":"Awakening, how to describe it.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-20T08:10:44-07:00","id":1094864,"title":"Awakening, how to describe it.","content":"What are some ways to describe a mage's awakening? I'm planning to start my game with my players awakening in the first session. Where in the core book does it detail this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10179-shadryx","name":"shadryx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-20T10:12:09-07:00","id":1094886,"title":"","content":"It doesn't. Not really. There are some depictions in relevant fiction of varying value. There is material in other, usually older books. It's not that you can't do it, but you REALLY have to decide how that sort of thing is going to work in your game. (TBH, Chronicles of Darkness Mage the Awakening has much more straightforward advice about it.)<br /> <br /> First question is how present/manifest are Avatars going to be in your game? How does this tie in with the number of dots in the Background? <br /> <br /> If Avatars are as present as Shadows are in Wraith or if that's what a high Avatar rating means, then you might want to think of full on dream-style, out of the mage's head, archetypical quest-like situations. (Almost like Harrowings, but in reverse.) Dreamscapes that occur at right angles to reality, somewhere between the mage's headspace and some Avatar-created not-really-a-hallucination that doesn't show up on any White Wolf schema of the cosmos. <br /> <br /> If Avatars aren't going to be popping up and nosing into the mage's business like bossy inscrutable invisible friends who hold the rip cord on a person even being a mage (or, if not having that kind of Avatar is what it means to have few dots in the Background), then an Awakening is going to be much lower key. Probably something along the lines of a &quot;Eureka&quot; moment while in the process of applying what will be their Focus in order change the world in a way that is less than normal THAT ENDS UP WORKING. &quot;Minhayana&quot; Buddhist style Awakening. (&quot;Before Enlightenment - Chop wood. Carry water. After enlighenment - Chop wood. Carry water). <br /> <br /> We've done it both ways. It really depends on the game. I think, on balance, the games with the first one (where EVERYONE gets the dreamscape, no matter the number of dots.... dots are more for how much the Avatar shows up at other times) seems a little more &quot;magey&quot; than the second in what we've done. I've RP'd through everyone's Awakenings AND Seekings from Arete 1 to whatever they start and made the whole thing a sort of Hero's Journey with each dot being further step. (They did like being able to breeze past the challenges from their Awakenings and previous Seekings as sorta &quot;window dressing&quot; on the way to the new challenge.) In that game, Seekings ended up being elaborate enough that it was a whole session devoted to THAT character and everyone else played characters in their little dream dance (sometimes their own typical character with an appropriate slant for the scene in question. Often someone else entirely or multiple someones . The other players would get briefing packets with sketch character write-ups.) <br /> <br /> In the current game, there is a sorta &quot;mission&quot; for each dot of Arete and there ends up being a problem facing the group that syncs with accomplishing that mission. Solve the problem and get the next dot of Arete. No Avatars involved at all. It's working really well, but it's not as &quot;magical&quot; in many ways....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-20T13:27:42-07:00","id":1094931,"title":"","content":"Thanks! I think I can run with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10179-shadryx","name":"shadryx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-20T18:01:13-07:00","id":1094981,"title":"","content":"Wow! I had a lot of examples queued up to give on both sides.... Great. Run with it!<br /> <br /> My next game, I plan on doing this as well. Setting up an Orphan game with the Awakenings occurring right after the first session (to establish the characters' &quot;normal side&quot; before the magic hits the fan and their lives begin to spiral out of control). Then moving on to having each character explore and create their Focus from the ground up.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T16:59:33-07:00","id":1095295,"title":"","content":"I think the key thing with the awakening is actually in the name of it.<br /> <br /> Awakening. When you're asleep. You're still aware. You're still thinking. But things aren't clear. they're muddled. Confusing. things happen and you don't draw the right conclusions because your brain just isn't working.<br /> <br /> Then you awaken. and what was once bewildering is clear as day.<br /> <br /> Mystical Awakening is like that. But while awake. An Awakened Mage is to a Sleeper, like a Sleeper is to a Sleeping Sleeper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}